# RamBlock build-time patch for UniXNU-merlinx (upstream RamBlock >= 00a6e5dd)
#
# Why this patch exists:
#   1. Upstream RamBlock forces disks > 2 GiB (e.g. merlinx's 120 GiB volatile
#      scratch-data.img) onto SeedDisk (isBig = true), which assumes a read-write
#      persistent UFS store (native_ufs_store_mode() == 2) and rejects all writes
#      with kIOReturnNotReady when no persistent store is present.
#   2. Upstream RamSparseDisk uses a flat pointer array pages[pageIndex], which
#      would need 240 MiB of metadata for a 120 GiB disk. The previous .o binary
#      patch masked pageIndex to 19 bits (2 GiB modulo wrap), causing silent
#      block aliasing and APFS obj_checksum_verify / SIGBUS (R2:a) corruption
#      once APFS allocated blocks past 2 GiB.
#
# What this patch does:
#   - Replaces RamSparseDisk's flat array with a 262,144-slot (4 MiB) 64-bit
#     open-addressing hash table keyed by full 64-bit pageIndex (zero aliasing
#     across any disk size up to 1 TiB, ~1 GiB resident 4K page capacity).
#   - Routes > 2 GiB disks through RamSparseDisk whenever no read-write UFS
#     persistent store is present, while preserving upstream SeedDisk + direct
#     mode unchanged if native_ufs_store_mode() == 2.
#   - Computes SHNGSEED2 (size + nonzero packed extents only) for > 2 GiB
#     sparse seeds so boot does not stall hashing 31M zero pages.
#
